      "title": "CMake: Don't necessarily trust pkg-config about Kerberos",
      "message": "CMake: Don't necessarily trust pkg-config about Kerberos\n\nWe search through each of the libraries that pkg-config gives\nus for Kerberos to find the full paths, because Debian and\nDebian derivatives like Ubuntu allowing installing the developer\npackages of MIT and Heimdal Kerberos simultaneously.\n\nIf we don't actually find the libraries with the hints that\npkg-config gave us, unset all the related variables and don't\nclaim we have Kerberos.\n\nThis is mostly useful when building with USE_STATIC (as happens with\n-DOSS_FUZZ=ON), because distributions generally don't ship static\nKerberos libraries. That's because MIT krb5 doesn't allow building\nstatic and shared libraries at the same time, so it's more of a pain\nfor distributions to build and package both.\n(https://github.com/krb5/krb5/blob/master/src/aclocal.m4#L836)\n\nFix #18931\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-03-23T21:08:47.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-01-23T06:51:36.000+00:00",
